course: dictionary
lesson: 1584
title: Chatter: talk, teeth and sounds
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: One word can have several meanings, and context tells you which one the writer means. «Stop chattering!» said in a classroom means stop talking quickly about small, unimportant things. The clue is the classroom: people talk there, and the teacher wants them quiet.
explain: Now read this: «Her teeth chattered in the icy wind.» Nothing is talking, so chatter must mean something else. Her teeth knock together because she is cold. Ask: what would fit here? Then try your meaning in the sentence and see if it still makes sense.
explain: Chatter can also be a noun, the sound itself. «The chatter of the café filled the room» means the noise of many people talking. Check how the word is used in the sentence, because a verb and a noun can have different jobs.
fact: Chatter can be a verb (to chatter) or a noun (chatter, the sound of chattering).
fact: «Chatter» means to talk quickly and a lot about small, unimportant things.
fact: When your teeth chatter, they knock together because you are very cold or scared.
fact: «Chatter» also means quick, repeated high sounds, like birds and monkeys make.
fact: «Idle chatter» means unimportant talk.
exercise: «Her teeth chattered in the icy wind.» What does chattered mean here? | *They knocked together because she was cold | They talked quickly about small things | They were tied together | They sang a happy song
exercise: «The birds chatter in the trees.» What does chatter mean here? | Fly very slowly | Gather in large flocks | *Make quick, repeated high sounds | Fall asleep in the branches
exercise: Mr Hale says «Stop chattering!» in class. What does he mean? | *Stop talking about unimportant things | Start singing | Stop shivering | Stop running
test: «The café was full of chatter.» What is chatter here? | A kind of cake | *The noise of people talking | A loud shout from the kitchen | A cold wind
test: Rahul says chatter always means being cold. Is he right? | No, it means happy | Yes, always | Only in winter | *No, it also means talking and bird sounds
exam: «Idle chatter» means what? | Silence in a library | Important news | *Unimportant talk | A loud shout
